{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Since Infancy: a past life story","html":"<article id='ja62'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Jātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Stories of Past Lives 62 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Itthivagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Women </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>2. Aṇḍabhūtajātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Since Infancy: a past life story </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Yaṁ brāhmaṇo avādesi, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The brahmin who played </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>vīṇaṁ samukhaveṭhito; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>the harp while blindfolded </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Aṇḍabhūtā bhatā bhariyā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>had raised his wife since infancy—</span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>tāsu ko jātu vissase”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>who would ever trust such women? </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>Aṇḍabhūtajātakaṁ dutiyaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
